coder › Implemented `match(pattern, path)` on branch `work/router-match`.

What changed:
- `src/router.ts` — implemented `match`: splits pattern/path on `/` after stripping leading/trailing slashes (so trailing slashes don't matter) and stripping `?query` from path; throws `TypeError` if a `*` segment appears anywhere but last; matches `:name` against exactly one non-empty segment, static segments by equality; a final `*` requires one or more remaining segments joined with `/` as `rest` (empty interior segments don't match); all param values go through `decodeURIComponent`. Noted one judgment call: interior empty segments (e.g. `//`) never match, for both `:name` and `*`.
- `src/router.test.ts` — new tests covering static match/mismatch, named params, segment-count mismatch, non-empty segment rule, percent-decoding (incl. `rest`), query-string ignoring, trailing slashes, `*` one-or-more and empty-after-`*` non-match, wildcard+param combo, and `TypeError` for non-final `*`.

